        "original_id": "9a60449f-fa3a-534f-95db-b66a338a1473",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eugène Ionesco, Paul Scott\n- Works: Amédée, or How to Get Rid of It, Oriflamme, The Raj Quartet, The Jewel in the Crown\n- Topics: French Avant-garde theatre, British Raj, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Eugène Ionesco was born as Eugen Ionescu on 26 November 1909 and became a Romanian-French playwright who wrote mostly in French.\n- Eugène Ionesco was one of the foremost figures of French Avant-garde theatre.\n- Paul Scott was born on 25 March 1920 and was an English novelist, playwright, and poet.\n- Eugène Ionesco wrote the play Amédée, or How to Get Rid of It in 1954 based on his earlier short story Oriflamme.\n- Paul Scott is best known for The Raj Quartet, a tetralogy of novels published from 1965 to 1975.\n- The Jewel in the Crown is a 1984 British television serial about the final days of the British Raj in India during and after World War II.\n- The Jewel in the Crown was based on The Raj Quartet novels by Paul Scott.\n- Paul Scott died on 1 March 1978.\n- Eugène Ionesco died on 28 March 1994.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
